`--tap-*` flags is passed through to `claude`.\n43\t\n44\t### CLI Flags\n45\t\n46\t| Flag | Default | Description |\n47\t|------|---------|-------------|\n48\t| `--tap-target` | auto-detect | Upstream API base URL |\n49\t| `--tap-port` | `0` (random) | Local proxy port (`0` = random available) |\n50\t| `--tap-output-dir` | `.traces` | Directory for JSONL trace files |\n51\t| `--tap-verbose` | `false` | Print debug logs |\n52\t\n53\t### Output Example\n54\t\n55\t```\n56\t🚀 Starting Claude Code: claude\n57\t   ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:52341\n58\t\n59\tproxy listening on http://127.0.0.1:52341\n60\t\n61\t⏳ Shutting down Claude Code... (Ctrl+C again to force)\n62\t\n63\t📋 Claude Code exited\n64\t   API calls:      12\n65\t   Input tokens:   45230\n66\t   Output tokens:  8192\n67\t   Cache read:     32000\n68\t   Cache create:   5000\n69\t   Trace: .traces/2026-05-19/trace_143052.jsonl\n70\t```\n71\t\n72\t## Architecture\n73\t\n74\t```\n75\tcmd/claude-tap/main.go          CLI entry — flag parsing, proxy lifecycle, child process management\n76\tinternal/\n77\t├── config/\n78\t│   ├── client.go               Client config (binary name, env vars, upstream detection)\n79\t│   └── claudeconfig.go         ~/.claude.json reader\n80\t├── proxy/\n81\t│   ├── reverse.go              Reverse proxy — request forwarding, SSE/non-SSE handling\n82\t│   ├── headers.go              Header filtering and sensitive value redaction\n83\t│   ├── paths.go                Allowed API path whitelist\n84\t│   └── netutil.go              Cross-platform network utilities\n85\t├── sse/\n86\t│   └── reassembler.go          SSE byte stream parser → complete API response reconstruction\n87\t├── trace/\n88\t│   └── writer.go               JSONL trace writer with token statistics\n89\t└── usage/\n90\t    └── normalize.go            Multi-provider token field normalization\n91\t```\n92\t\n93\t### Data Flow\n94\t\n95\t1. CLI parses flags, detects upstream URL, starts local proxy\n96\t2. Proxy intercepts requests, forwards to upstream API\n97\t3. For streaming responses, `SSEReassembler` reassembles SSE chunks into a complete response object\n98\t4. Each request/response pair is recorded as one JSONL line via `TraceWriter`\n99\t5. On exit, a usage summary is printed (API calls, token counts by category)\n100\t\n101\t## Supported API Paths\n102\t\n103\tThe proxy only forwards recognized paths and rejects everything else (scanners, crawlers) with 404:\n104\t\n105\t- `/v1/messages` — Anthropic Messages API\n106\t- `/v1/responses` — OpenAI Responses API\n107\t- `/v1/chat/completions` — OpenAI Chat Completions\n108\t- `/v1/models`, `/v1/embeddings`, `/v1/files` — OpenAI utilities\n109\t- `/v1beta/`, `/v1/` — Google Gemini API\n110\t- `/coding/v1/` — Kimi API\n111\t\n112\t## Development\n113\t\n114\t```bash\n115\t# Tidy dependencies\n116\tgo mod tidy\n117\t\n118\t# Run directly without building\n119\tgo run ./cmd/claude-tap claude\n120\t\n121\t# Format\n122\tgofmt -w .\n123\t```\n124\t"}]}
