[2026-05-26 23:19:37] [INFO] [SubagentStop] Input: {"session_id":"6b6f69d3-9e1d-4780-a581-98aedcfada98","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\6b6f69d3-9e1d-4780-a581-98aedcfada98.jsonl","cwd":"D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk","permission_mode":"acceptEdits","agent_id":"a3878355f1811bbab","agent_type":"Explore","hook_event_name":"SubagentStop","stop_hook_active":false,"agent_transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\6b6f69d3-9e1d-4780-a581-98aedcfada98\\subagents\\agent-a3878355f1811bbab.jsonl","last_assistant_message":"Based on my exploration of the claude_tap_plus Go project, here's a concise summary of each area:\n\n## 1. **Proxy Interception Flow (internal/proxy/)**\n\nThe proxy works as a reverse proxy that intercepts AI CLI API traffic:\n\n- **Request Flow**: \n  - Starts HTTP server on local port (random if unspecified)\n  - Accepts only API paths from `AllowedPathPrefixes` (Anthropic, OpenAI, Gemini, Kimi APIs)\n  - Filters hop-by-hop headers and redacts sensitive values\n  - Extracts `session_id` from request metadata\n\n- **Response Handling**:\n  - For streaming requests (stream=true): uses SSE reassembler to reconstruct complete responses\n  - For non-streaming: decompresses response body if needed\n  - Records complete request/response pairs to JSONL trace\n\n## 2. **Data Captured in Traces (internal/trace/)**\n\nEach API call is recorded as a JSON line with:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"timestamp\": \"...\",\n  \"request_id\": \"...\",\n  \"session_id\": \"...\",\n  \"turn\": number,\n  \"duration_ms\": number,\n  \"request\": {\n    \"method\": \"POST\",\n    \"path\": \"/v1/messages\",\n    \"headers\": {...},\n    \"body\": {...}\n  },\n  \"response\": {\n    \"status\": 200,\n    \"headers\": {...},\n    \"body\": {...},\n    \"sse_events\": [...] // for streaming\n  },\n  \"upstream_base_url\": \"...\"\n}\n```\n\n**Token Statistics**: Tracks input/output tokens, cache read/create tokens across all calls with model breakdown.\n\n## 3. **CLI Lifecycle (cmd/claude-tap/main.go)**\n\nThe main flow:\n\n1. **Parse** --tap-* flags and collect remaining args for Claude\n2. **Detect** upstream URL (env var → config → default)\n3. **Create** trace writer with timestamped filename\n4. **Start** reverse proxy on local port\n5. **Launch** Claude Code as child process with proxy URL in env\n6. **Signal handling**: Forward SIGINT/SIGTERM to child\n7. **Wait** for child exit, then stop proxy\n8. **Print** usage summary\n\n## 4. **Session Sync (internal/session/)**\n\nThree session commands:\n\n- **session-push**: Collects session files from `~/.claude/projects/{slug}/` to local storage\n  - Detects project name from git remote or cwd basename\n  - Copies `.jsonl` session files and subagents directories\n  - Updates `meta.json` with session metadata (timestamps, models, branch info)\n  \n- **session-pull**: Restores sessions from local storage to `~/.claude/`\n- **session-status**: Shows collected sessions and their details\n\n## 5. **Config/Upstream URL Detection (internal/config/)**\n\nPriority order for detecting upstream target:\n\n1. Environment variable (ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL)\n2. ~/.claude.json config (reads both top-level `base_url` and `env.anthropic_base_url`)\n3. Default target (https://api.anthropic.com)\n\nChild process environment:\n- Inherits current env\n- Clears proxy nesting env vars (CLAUDECODE, CLAUDE_CODE_SSE_PORT)\n- Sets ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL to local proxy URL\n\n## Proxy Lifecycle Summary\n\n**Start** → Parse flags → Create trace writer → Start proxy server → Launch Claude child → Intercept requests → Record traces → **Stop** → Print summary\n\nThe proxy acts as a man-in-the-middle, intercepting all API calls, reconstructing streaming responses, and maintaining a complete audit trail while being completely transparent to the user.","background_tasks":[],"session_crons":[]}
